            harvest_time_unparsed: "late early to mid-season",
            description: "Casscles, Plocher, and Trzaskos describe La Crescent as a University of Minnesota 2002 St. Pepin seedling that is easy to grow, moderate to vigorous, somewhat resistant to fungus diseases, and able to make moderate yields on lighter soils or heavier yields on richer soils. Source notes: relatively early bud break with secondary crop potential after late frost, about 24 Brix, firm to high acid, floral apricot-driven wines with apple, peach, tropical fruit, pineapple, mango, and honey notes, and dry to semi-sweet wine styles"
