        },
        {
            type: "Grape",
            name: "St. Pepin",
            category: "Minnesota white grape varieties for the Northeast",
            harvest_time_unparsed: "early mid-season, ten days to two weeks before La Crosse",
            description: "Casscles, Plocher, and Trzaskos describe St. Pepin as an early Elmer Swenson hybrid introduced in 1983, a sibling of La Crosse, and the seed parent of La Crescent. Source notes: moderately to very vigorous vines with moderate to good productivity, somewhat open canopy, some resistance to most fungus diseases but susceptibility to powdery mildew, female flowers requiring nearby compatible grapes for fruit set, 20 to 24 Brix, relatively low balanced acids, and fruitier Riesling-like wine character"
        },
        {
            type: "Grape",
            name: "Brianna",
            category: "Minnesota white grape varieties for the Northeast",
            harvest_time_unparsed: "early mid-season",
            description: "Casscles, Plocher, and Trzaskos describe Brianna as an Elmer Swenson selection from 1989 with table-grape and winemaking uses. Source notes: medium to high vigor, moderate resistance to most fungus diseases but weaker resistance to black rot and botrytis, possible crown gall susceptibility, sulfur tolerance, tolerance of hot and cold extremes, secondary crop potential after late spring frost, green-gold thick-skinned berries, semi-sweet pineapple and tropical wine character, drier-wine grapefruit, banana, and mango notes, and value for blending and dessert wines"
        },
        {
            type: "Grape",
            name: "Louise Swenson",
