            harvest_time_unparsed: "early mid-season",
            description: "Casscles, Plocher, and Trzaskos describe Louise Swenson as an Elmer Swenson white grape introduced in 2001 with help from Tom Plocher and Bob Parke. Source notes: medium vigor, good fungus disease resistance with possible anthracnose susceptibility, sensitivity to sulfur, moderate production, dislike of droughty or light sandy soils, late bud break that helps avoid spring frost, easy field management, and soft balanced wines with pear and honey aromas that can blend well with Prairie Star"
        },
        {
            type: "Grape",
            name: "Prairie Star",
            category: "Minnesota white grape varieties for the Northeast",
