            description: "Casscles, Plocher, and Trzaskos describe Prairie Star as an Elmer Swenson selection introduced in 2001 with help from Tom Plocher and Bob Parke. Source notes: vigorous semi-upright vines, general fungus disease resistance with moderate resistance to black rot and anthracnose, possible poor fruit set, wind-sensitive young shoots, better production on heavier soils or when grafted, 20 to 22 Brix with proportionate acid, and neutral to somewhat floral wines with body, mouthfeel, and finish useful for blending"
        },
        {
            type: "Grape",
            name: "Swenson White",
            category: "Minnesota white grape varieties for the Northeast",
            harvest_time_unparsed: "late mid-season to late",
            description: "Casscles, Plocher, and Trzaskos describe Swenson White as an Elmer Swenson white grape introduced in 1994. Source notes: medium to large loose to well-filled clusters, large light-green berries with some yellow, thick skins that allow late-harvest or ice-wine hang time and reduce bird and insect damage, good fungus disease resistance except some susceptibility to downy and powdery mildew, healthy growth, mid-season bud break with small secondary crop potential, possible need for cluster thinning, sugars up to about 22 Brix, moderate acidity, and floral St. Pepin-like wines with substantial fruit and mild labrusca elements"
